<section class="section press-feature" id="in-the-news" aria-labelledby="press-feature-title">
  <div class="press-feature__masthead">
    <span>ColumbiaWalks in the news</span>
    <time datetime="2026-08-12">August 12, 2026</time>
  </div>
  <div class="press-feature__layout">
    <div class="press-feature__copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">Front-page coverage · The Columbia Chronicle</p>
      <h2 id="press-feature-title">Pedestrian safety takes center stage at Borough Council.</h2>
      <p>Following ColumbiaWalks developer Robert Thompson’s August 11 address to Columbia Borough Council, <em>The Columbia Chronicle</em> reported on the community’s urgent call for safer streets. The coverage highlights requests for a comprehensive pedestrian-safety plan, stronger crosswalk enforcement, infrastructure review, and a full examination of pedestrian incidents and complaints.</p>
      <a class="button press-feature__button" href="https://thecolumbiachronicle.com/website-news/tragedy-public-safety-and-heated-debate-dominate-columbia-borough-meeting/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the Chronicle coverage <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      <p class="press-feature__note">Independent reporting by <em>The Columbia Chronicle</em>. The article opens on the newspaper’s website.</p>
    </div>
    <aside class="press-feature__summary" aria-label="Requests highlighted in the coverage">
      <p>What the Council address called for</p>
      <ul>
        <li>A comprehensive pedestrian-safety plan</li>
        <li>Stronger crosswalk enforcement</li>
        <li>Infrastructure, incident, and complaint review</li>
      </ul>
    </aside>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="section wgal-feature" aria-labelledby="wgal-feature-title">
  <div class="wgal-feature__copy">
    <p class="eyebrow">Local television coverage · WGAL News 8</p>
    <h2 id="wgal-feature-title">Columbia residents call for action after deadly crash.</h2>
    <p>WGAL's August 13 report connects the deaths of Eric and Donna Lutz at Third and Chestnut streets with residents' longstanding concerns about speeding, unsafe crossings, and the need for visible enforcement. The coverage also examines practical ideas raised by neighbors, including improved markings, additional signs, pedestrian-activated flashing beacons, and targeted monitoring at dangerous intersections.</p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="button primary" href="{{@site.url}}/wgal-coverage/">View the coverage summary and media</a>
      <a class="text-link" href="https://www.wgal.com/article/columbia-residents-urge-action-after-fatal-crash-at-intersection/73418945" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read and watch on WGAL →</a>
    </div>
    <p class="wgal-feature__credit">Reporting by Maegan Summers for WGAL News 8. ColumbiaWalks does not host or alter WGAL's video footage.</p>
  </div>
  <aside class="wgal-feature__facts" aria-label="WGAL coverage highlights">
    <span>Coverage highlights</span>
    <strong>2 official videos</strong>
    <ul>
      <li>Residents describe speeding and dangerous driving</li>
      <li>Neighbors propose signs, markings, and flashing beacons</li>
      <li>Police discuss possible targeted intersection enforcement</li>
    </ul>
  </aside>
</section>
