<section class="section mission" id="mission"><div><p class="eyebrow">Built for neighbors</p><h2>Turn everyday observations into useful community data.</h2><p>Cracked sidewalks, blocked crosswalks, poor lighting, speeding, and inaccessible curb ramps are easy to notice but difficult to track. ColumbiaWalks keeps those observations organized so recurring trouble spots become visible.</p></div><ol class="steps"><li><b>1</b><span><strong>Choose one category</strong>Sidewalk, driver, crosswalk, or another safety issue.</span></li><li><b>2</b><span><strong>Add a clear photo</strong>Document the condition without putting yourself in danger.</span></li><li><b>3</b><span><strong>Confirm GPS and submit</strong>Add an optional comment only when it helps explain the picture.</span></li></ol></section>
<section class="section pedestrian-profile-callout" id="pedestrian-profile" aria-labelledby="pedestrian-profile-title"><div><p class="eyebrow">New community questionnaire</p><h2 id="pedestrian-profile-title">What is walking in Columbia like for you?</h2><p>Share an anonymous Pedestrian Profile to help us understand residents’ walking habits, favorite and least favorite streets, accessibility needs, and the changes that would make walking easier. Every question is optional.</p><a class="button primary" href="{{@site.url}}/report/#pedestrian-profile">Complete a Pedestrian Profile</a></div><aside aria-label="Pedestrian Profile privacy and timing"><strong>Optional. Anonymous. Useful.</strong><span>No account, name, or exact address is requested.</span><span>Answer only the questions you are comfortable sharing.</span></aside></section>
<section class="section report-callout"><div><p class="eyebrow">Safety reporting</p><h2>See a problem? Put it on the map.</h2><p>No account is required. Quick Report asks only for one broad category, a photograph, an optional comment, and a confirmed GPS location. Use Full Report when the incident needs detailed questions or additional documentation.</p><a class="button primary" href="{{@site.url}}/report/">Open the reporting tool</a></div><div class="badge-panel"><img src="{{asset "columbiawalks-badge.svg"}}" alt="ColumbiaWalks badge"><span>Safer streets<br>start with a clear picture.</span></div></section>
<section class="section split"><article><p class="eyebrow">Explore on foot</p><h2>Historic Columbia Walking Tours</h2><p>Discover Columbia’s architecture, river heritage, parks, and neighborhood stories through a separate collection of self-guided walks.</p><a class="text-link" href="{{@site.url}}/historic-walks/">Explore historic walks →</a></article><article class="river"><p class="eyebrow">Walk the river</p><h2>Northwest Lancaster County River Trail</h2><p>Columbia is the southern gateway to miles of paved trail, river views, and connections to our region’s industrial history.</p></article></section>
<section class="section cw-contact-callout"><p class="eyebrow">Meet your neighbors</p><h2>Let’s make walking better, together.</h2><p>ColumbiaWalks was founded by Callie Jo Thompson and Robert Burton Thompson V. Get in touch with a question, an idea, or feedback about the project.</p><a class="button primary" href="{{@site.url}}/contact/">Contact Us</a></section>
<section class="section news"><p class="eyebrow">Project updates</p><h2>From ColumbiaWalks</h2><div class="post-grid">{{#foreach posts limit="3"}}<article><p>{{date published_at format="MMMM D, YYYY"}}</p><h3><a href="{{url}}">{{title}}</a></h3><p>{{excerpt words="24"}}</p></article>{{else}}<p>Updates from the ColumbiaWalks project will appear here.</p>{{/foreach}}</div></section>
